My shopping bags are full and heavy.
I am also a little cold in my jacket.
I need a break.
I see a small cart with coffee.
A man stands behind the coffee machine.
I walk over to the cart.
"Good morning, I would like a coffee," I say.
"Gladly."
"With milk and sugar?" the seller asks.
"Only with milk, please."
"How much is that?"
"That is three euros," he answers.
I give him the money.
He gives me the warm cup.
"Thank you very much and have a nice day," he says.
"Thank you, same to you," I say.
I walk to a small high table at the edge.
I put the shopping bags on the ground.
I drink the coffee.
It is nice and warm and tastes good.
Many people walk past.
I watch the people and enjoy my break.
